  "problem": "Simplify the expression $P\u2228(P\u21d2Q).$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operation\n\n- First, we use that $X\u21d2Y\u2261\u00acX\u2228Y:$\n\n$$\nP\u2228(P\u21d2Q)\u2261P\u2228(\u00acP\u2228Q)\n$$\n\n- Next, we use the associative law:\n\n$$\nP\u2228(\u00acP\u2228Q)\u2261(P\u2228\u00acP)\u2228Q\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the fact that the disjunction of an expression and its negation is a tautology:\n\n$$\n(P\u2228\u00acP)\u2228Q\u2261\\text{t}\u2228Q\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the disjunction of an expression and a tautology gives a tautology:\n\n$$\n\\text{t}\u2228Q\u2261\\text{t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P\u2228(P\u21d2Q) & \u2261\\text{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
